# L §5.14.1 next, L §5 a form defined by another (tally 2.1.7 R6, issue #145; G4): next(pays, d) is
# first(m in pays over d ..) ties by m.day, so a decision's `reads pays` is a read it makes; load passes, and the
# run meets the binding's own reach past the decision's day (RUN-FUTURE). 2.1.6's refcore refused LOAD-READS fee
# declares reads pays and never reads it.
=== m.tally
model g4
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-03-31
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
kind pays: event certain
  leg cash: DUK
place konto: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2025-01-01..
move pay[m in months]: pays
  on end_of(m) - 1 day
  when bal(konto) > 0 or pos(m) > 1
  reads konto
  leg cash from world to konto amount 1
move fee[m in months]: transfers
  on end_of(m)
  when next(pays, start_of(m)).day < end_of(m)
  reads pays
  leg cash from world to konto amount 1
ask q: bal(konto, 2025-03-31)
=== expect
q: refused: RUN-FUTURE a decision on 2025-02-01 binds over pays through the end, after its day
  cut 2025-01-01
